==================================================================
OBSERVATIONS (not criterion failures)
==================================================================
O1. In S5's sequence 1, after the mutation that RESOLVES the overlap, the live
    region still reads "Pattern overlap warning dismissed." rather than "".
    lastWarningsText was set to '' at dismiss time and effectiveText is also
    '' on that call, so the same-text guard correctly skips the write and the
    stale confirmation copy lingers. It asserts a dismissal, not an active
    warning, so it does not violate point 16 as written; noted for
    checker-a11y, whose lane this is.
O2. scriptBlockRE is case-sensitive and stops at the first literal
    "</script>". Both are under-strips (false failure, never false pass) and
    neither is reachable from today's templates. Not a finding.

==================================================================
BOTTOM LINE
==================================================================
Items (b), (c), (d) and (e) are done properly and I proved each one by
mutation, not by reading. Item (a) is a genuine, working fix -- I ran the
shipped JS and both point-16 defects are gone, and the whitespace-padding bug
the worker found alongside it is real and fixed too. But criterion 1 asks
whether a regression turns something red, and it does not: restoring the
byte-identical pre-S5 accounts.html leaves `go test ./...` at exit 0, and
deleting syncWarnings entirely leaves the accounts package green. The work is
correct and unguarded. What is missing is one executable check, inside the
repo, that fails when syncWarnings' dismissal ordering regresses.
